    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a tool rather than an abstract concept for me—useful but not overwhelming. I enjoy solving problems logically and find physics’ equations intriguing when broken down, especially since my love for economics requires quantitative reasoning. My background in vocational training helped me develop patterns quickly, though I’d admit I prefer concrete examples over pure theory.",
