    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Once, while revising algebra, I used an online step-by-step solver (like Wolfram Alpha) to verify solutions. It saved time and reduced frustration when stuck on factorization or inequalities. The downside? Over-reliance made me less confident solving from scratch—so I now balance it with paper-and-pencil practice.",
